From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 10:55:58 -0400
Subject: import: an Arc user's sidebar comes across, Spaces, essentials, pins
 and folders, every tab unloaded

spaces::ParseArcSidebar reads Arc's StorableSidebar.json into a plan
(Spaces with their icon and the nearest Stedding swatch, the essentials,
per Space the pinned and unpinned items with lists as folders) and
ApplyArcImport applies it to a window: a lone unnamed default Space is
taken over by the first Arc Space, the essentials are capped at twelve,
loose pinned items become Space-pinned tabs with their home, lists become
folders, and every tab is a restored navigation entry marked discarded so
a large sidebar costs nothing until a tab is opened. The file is read
through a copy since Arc rewrites it while running; the flow says when Arc
is running; Arc's per-Space profile binding is dropped and named in the
summary; a second import adds nothing (Arc's ids are kept in the profile).
Entry points: the welcome flow's import step, chrome://settings/stedding
under the Spaces list, and a bar action (docs/features/import.md I1-I4,
I8-I12).

Why: docs/ROUND6-PLAN.md wave 3, R6-22: the first thing an Arc user does.
Removable when: Chromium's importer knows Arc's sidebar, or Arc ships an
export.
